<title>SINGAPORE: Material Handling full year net profit up.</title>
<headline>Material Handling full year net profit up.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full-year ended June 30 1996</p>
<p>(in million of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			  0.09   vs   3.16 (loss)</p>
<p>    Earnings per share (cents)    0.19   vs   7.20 (loss)</p>
<p>    Dividend (percent)		2.50   vs    nil</p>
<p>    Turnover			   23.94   vs  17.37</p>
<p>    Interest income		   0.03   vs   0.09</p>
<p>    Interest expense		  0.26   vs   0.29</p>
<p>    Depreciation/amortisation     0.85   vs   0.90</p>
<p>    Associates			  0.008  vs   0.01 (loss)</p>
<p>    Pretax				0.03   vs   3.00 (loss)</p>
<p>    Tax				   0.07   vs   0.17</p>
<p>Note- Material Handling Engineering Ltd said its return to profit was due to higher productivity and income realised.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
</text>
